# Vendor property contexts for the MediaTek / OPPO blobs.
#
# Android 10 has no equivalent of the stock 8.1
# /vendor/etc/selinux/nonplat_property_contexts (the stock image shipped 70
# rules). Without a vendor file every persist.* key the blobs use falls back to
# whatever the platform claims, and AOSP's
#     neverallow { domain -init -vendor_init } default_prop:property_service set;
# (system/sepolicy/public/domain.te) means no HAL can *write* a default_prop key.
# Under the current permissive bring-up policy that only logs; on an enforcing
# build those setprop calls fail and the related feature silently stays off.
#
# This file labels only the families AOSP does not already cover. Deliberately
# NOT re-declared, because AOSP's own rules are already correct and a second,
# different type for the same prefix would be a conflict:
#
#   persist.radio.*        -> radio_prop          (rild may set it)
#   persist.bluetooth.*    -> bluetooth_prop
#   persist.debug.*        -> persist_debug_prop
#   persist.logd.*         -> logd_prop / log_tag_prop
#   persist.audio.*        -> audio_prop
#   persist.sys.locale     -> system_prop  (framework-owned)
#   persist.sys.timezone   -> system_prop  (framework-owned)
#   persist.sys.usb.config -> system_prop  (framework-owned)
#   persist.service.bdroid.* -> bluetooth_prop
#
# Framework-owned persist.sys.* keys are left alone as well; only the vendor
# sub-families below are claimed. All of these resolve to mtk_persist_prop,
# which device.te grants for reading to every domain (get_prop) and for writing
# to the vendor daemons that own them (set_prop).

# --- MTK exception / dump (aee) ---
